# TODO
## Authentication & authorization

- [ ] Authenticate submitters (session/JWT from the website); only they can POST /messages
- [ ] Moderator/admin role: only they can approve, reject, list messages and see sender_ip
- [ ] Per-printer API tokens (stored hashed in `printers`); printers can only poll/claim/report status
- [ ] Group routes in chi behind role-specific middleware

## Approval flow

- [ ] SubmitMessage: set initial status (pending / awaiting_approval) based on source instead of always pending
- [ ] Derive source from the caller's identity instead of hardcoding SourceWeb in createMessage
- [ ] Add a reject route (StatusRejected)
- [ ] Fix ApproveMessage race (read-then-write): replace UpdateMessageStatus with an atomic *TransitionStatus(id, from, to)* using `UPDATE ... WHERE id = $2 AND status = $3`; on no rows, look up the message to return ErrNotFound vs ErrInvalidStatus
- [ ] Idem for RejectMessage
- [ ] Set approved_at / claimed_at / printed_at on the matching transitions

## Printer side

- [ ] Add StatusClaimed to the Go model (exists in the DB constraint)
- [ ] Printer store/service (the `printers` table is unused)
- [ ] Atomic claim endpoint: `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, set printer_id, claimed_at, attempts+1
- [ ] Status reporting endpoints: printing -> printed, or failed with last_error
- [ ] Heartbeat endpoint updating printers.last_seen_at / last_job_at
- [ ] Recover stuck claims: back to pending after a timeout, give up after max attempts

## Security hardening

- [ ] Strip control characters (except) from content to prevent ESC/POS command injection; filter again on the Pi
- [ ] Rate limiting per user and per IP
- [ ] Only use middleware.RealIP behind a trusted reverse proxy (X-Forwarded-For is spoofable)

